#**
The default rendering for the editor's live-preview shell, used when the
weblog's theme does not supply a template named _preview.

Deliberately not a page: no header, no nav, no pager, no entry chrome. The
shell exists so an author sees their prose in the weblog's own stylesheet
while they type, and the editor fills #previewArticle over postMessage (see
#showPreviewShellScript). A theme that ships its own _preview names the
classes its reading column is actually styled through; this one cannot know
them, so it uses neutral roller-preview-* names and gets the stylesheet, the
measure-free defaults and the shortcode assets right instead.
*#
<!DOCTYPE html>
## lang must be a BCP-47 tag; $model.weblog.locale is Java's stored form
## ("en_US"), which no user agent recognises. WeblogWrapper#getLanguageTag
## does the conversion -- same as templates/weblog/page.vm.
<html lang="$model.weblog.getLanguageTag()">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    ## The bundled themes' standard policy with one directive changed:
    ## frame-ancestors 'self' rather than 'none', because this document is
    ## MEANT to be framed -- by the editor, on the same origin. Everything
    ## else stays byte-identical (font-src included, since a theme may
    ## self-host a webfont) so a preview never renders under a policy the
    ## published page does not have.
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src * data:; frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; connect-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'">
    <title>Preview</title>
    #if($model.weblog.stylesheet)<link rel="stylesheet" href="$model.weblog.stylesheet">#end
    <style>
    .roller-preview { margin: 0; }
    .roller-preview-main { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem 3rem; }
    </style>
    ## The same ones the themes call, in the same order and for the same
    ## reason: #showEmbedAssets and the content assets bind on
    ## DOMContentLoaded, and the gallery and map stylesheets arriving at the
    ## end of <body> would be a flash of unstyled gallery/map. #showAudienceAssets is deliberately absent -- a
    ## [contact] or [subscribe] form in a preview would be a live, posting
    ## form on unsaved text.
    #showGalleryGridStyles()
    #showGalleryAssets()
    #showMapAssets()
    #showContentAssets()
    #showEmbedAssets()
    #showPreviewShellScript()
</head>
<body class="roller-preview">
<main class="roller-preview-main">
    <article id="previewArticle" class="roller-preview-prose"></article>
</main>
</body>
</html>
